---
.title = "iroh: encrypted peer-to-peer",
.description = "iroh carries CapTP over encrypted QUIC with discovery and NAT traversal, and names each peer by a self-authenticating key rather than a host and port.",
.date = @date("2026-06-17T00:00:00"),
.author = "Jim Isaacs",
.layout = "page.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

iroh is the transport that lets two peers find each other without a fixed
address or a server in the middle. A session's bytes ride
[QUIC](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000.html) carried by
[iroh](https://www.iroh.computer/), and a peer is named by a self-authenticating
key rather than a `host:port`. Everything above the wire stays the same OCapN
pancake speaks over TCP. Switching to iroh changes how a peer is addressed and
how it is reached: discovery, relays, and NAT traversal come with the channel.
For a direct TCP route between pancake peers that only needs encryption, prefer
[Noise]($link.page('transports/noise')) (`noise-tcp`) instead.

Goblins ships no iroh netlayer. Live Goblins-over-iroh
(`zig build goblins-iroh`) uses the adapter in `conformance/goblins-peer/`.
Prefer [onion]($link.page('transports/onion')) when both sides should run
unmodified upstream transports.

## Dial

The iroh dial examples are the transport-page view of the same binding
snippets. Configuration belongs to the provider; the operation supplies only
the locator and any per-connect options.

```=html
<!-- site-examples:dial:iroh GENERATED by `zig build gen-site-examples`; edits are overwritten -->
```
> []($block.attrs('code-tabs'))
> **Zig**
> ```zig
> const std = @import("std");
> const pancake = @import("pancake");
> const iroh = @import("iroh");
>
> pub fn example(io: std.Io, allocator: std.mem.Allocator) !void {
>     // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
>     var iroh_resident = try iroh.Resident.init(io, null, .{ .reachability = .discovery });
>     defer iroh_resident.deinit();
>     const netlayers = [_]pancake.net.netlayer.Netlayer{iroh_resident.netlayer()};
>     const node_id = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>";
>     const partner = iroh.locator(node_id);
> ```
> **TypeScript**
> ```ts
> import { Runtime } from "@pancake/runtime";
> import { locator, provider, Reachability } from "@pancake/iroh";
>
> // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> const nodeId = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>";
> const partner = locator(nodeId);
>
> await using runtime = await Runtime.open({
> 	providers: [provider({ reachability: Reachability.Discovery })],
> });
> ```
> **Browser**
> ```ts
> import { init } from "@pancake/web";
>
> const web = await init({
> 	wasm: fetch("/pancake_host.wasm"),
> 	relayUrl: (locator) => `wss://relay.example/?locator=${encodeURIComponent(locator)}`,
> });
> await using runtime = web.runtime;
> // `@pancake/iroh` loads native FFI, so a page parses the locator on the web runtime.
> const partner = web.parseLocator("ocapn://<64 lowercase hex characters>.iroh");
> ```
> **Python**
> ```python
> from pancake import Runtime
> from pancake.iroh import IrohConfig, Reachability, locator, provider
>
> # DISCOVERY resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> node_id = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>"
> partner = locator(node_id)
>
> async with Runtime.open(
>     provider=provider(IrohConfig(Reachability.DISCOVERY))
> ) as runtime:
> ```
> **Rust**
> ```rust
> use pancake::iroh::{self, Reachability};
> use pancake::{Argument, ConnectOptions, PendingWork, Runtime, RuntimeConfig};
>
> // Discovery resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> // Cargo.toml: pancake = { …, features = ["iroh"] }
> let node_id = "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>";
> let partner = iroh::locator(node_id, None);
>
> let runtime = Runtime::open(RuntimeConfig::providers([iroh::provider(iroh::Config::new(
>     Reachability::Discovery,
> ))]))
> .await?;
> ```
> **Racket**
> ```scheme
> (require "pancake.rkt"
>          "pancake-iroh.rkt")
>
> ;; IROH-REACH-DISCOVERY resolves a bare iroh node ID without an address hint.
> (define node-id "<64 lowercase hex characters from the server>")
> (define partner (iroh-locator node-id))
>
> (define runtime
>   (open-runtime
>    #:providers (list (iroh-provider (make-iroh-config IROH-REACH-DISCOVERY)))))
> ```
